{"last_link_id": 39, "nodes": [{"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "audio", "links": [27], "label": "audio", "type": "AUDIO", "localized_name": "audio"}], "size": [624.6138192060666, 1174.6281382259779], "pos": [4213.829815230564, 35.82169972018672], "widgets_values": ["[{\"speaker\":\"Lois\",\"text\":\"Okay, everyone, focus for a second. Breeze TTS 2 inside ComfyUI is seriously impressive. You can clone a voice, design a completely new one, and it can run on cards with as little as 8GB of VRAM.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Peter\",\"text\":\"Lois, I have been focused for six minutes. That's basically a personal record.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Brian\",\"text\":\"The impressive part is that saganaki22 made the custom nodes and the INT8 converted quantizations, so you're not necessarily sacrificing your entire GPU just to run TTS.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Stewie\",\"text\":\"Marvelous. Technology has finally reached the point where even Peter can operate it without setting fire to the computer.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Peter\",\"text\":\"Hey! You just add each speaker with the Breeze Speaker node, upload some audio, and choose whether ASR is on or off. That's easier than ordering a pizza.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Lois\",\"text\":\"And if you already have the transcript, you can provide it yourself. Or, if you don't want to clone a real voice, you can simply describe the voice you want with instructions.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Peter\",\"text\":\"Like a voice that sounds handsome, intelligent, and extremely good at eating sandwiches.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Brian\",\"text\":\"Peter, that's not voice design. That's wishful thinking.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Stewie\",\"text\":\"Although the machine may be powerful enough to manufacture the illusion.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Lois\",\"text\":\"Then you connect all your speakers to the Multi Speaker node. For the dialogue, you can paste JSON generated by an LLM, or just write it normally yourself.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Brian\",\"text\":\"Exactly. So you can have multiple cloned or designed speakers in one workflow and control the whole conversation without manually stitching everything together afterward.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Peter\",\"text\":\"Wait, so I can make Peter, Brian, Lois, and Stewie all talk in the same workflow? Holy crap, we're basically actors now.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Stewie\",\"text\":\"No, Peter. Actors can read a script without requiring technical support from their mother.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Peter\",\"text\":\"Whatever. Eight gigs, voice cloning, voice design, ASR, transcripts, JSON, multiple speakers. This thing is awesome.\"},{\"speaker\":\"Lois\",\"text\":\"For once, Peter is actually right. Breeze TTS 2 with these ComfyUI nodes gives you a ridiculous amount of control in one workflow.\"}]\n", 0.3, 1500, 0.9, 50, 1, 1.1, 0.9, 50, 1, 1638845876, "randomize"], "inputs": [{"name": "breeze_model", "link": 31, "label": "breeze_model", "type": "BREEZE_TTS2_MODEL", "localized_name": "breeze_model"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "speaker_1", "link": 34, "label": "speaker_1", "type": "BREEZE_SPEAKER", "localized_name": "speaker_1"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "speaker_2", "link": 35, "label": "speaker_2", "type": "BREEZE_SPEAKER", "localized_name": "speaker_2"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "speaker_3", "link": 36, "label": "speaker_3", "type": "BREEZE_SPEAKER", "localized_name": "speaker_3"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "speaker_4", "link": 37, "label": "speaker_4", "type": "BREEZE_SPEAKER", "localized_name": "speaker_4"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "speaker_5", "label": "speaker_5", "type": "BREEZE_SPEAKER", "localized_name": "speaker_5"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "speaker_6", "label": "speaker_6", "type": "BREEZE_SPEAKER", "localized_name": "speaker_6"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "speaker_7", "label": "speaker_7", "type": "BREEZE_SPEAKER", "localized_name": "speaker_7"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "speaker_8", "label": "speaker_8", "type": "BREEZE_SPEAKER", "localized_name": "speaker_8"}, {"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "link": 38, "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_nam